    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, with every value derived from it following along:\n\n**Core change \u2014 `CustomerCodeGenerator`** (`service/CustomerCodeGenerator.java`)\n- Now produces `<REGION>-<HASH8>`: `REGION` is the region code and `HASH8` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`. The old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` sequence format is gone.\n\n**Region wiring \u2014 `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** (`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`)\n- Resolves the region via `LocalityResolver.regionFor(postcode, city)` (postcode preferred, city fallback) and passes it plus the already-normalized telephone and last name to the generator. Dropped the per-city sequence computation; the `countOwnersInCity` javadoc was trimmed to its remaining purpose (the capacity limit).\n\n**Locality derivation \u2014 `Owner.getLocality`** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- Now reads the region back out of the `customerCode` (the segment before the first `-`), so locality is anchored to the same region-and-hash identity, with a direct postcode/city fallback before the code is assigned.\n\n**Values built from the code** followed automatically because they already consume `customerCode`:\n- `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and `checkDigit` (Luhn over the code's digits) now reflect the new code with no logic change.\n- The create audit record in `OwnerAuditLogger` logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it emits the new identity (verified in the run: `AUDIT - Owner created: ... customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\n**Shared utility \u2014 `Sha256Hex`** (`service/Sha256Hex.java`, new)\n- Extracted the SHA-256\u2192upper-hex-prefix logic into one place; both `CustomerCodeGenerator` and `HouseholdIdGenerator` now reuse it instead of duplicating the digest code.\n\n**Docs \u2014 `openapi.yml`**\n- Updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` descriptions/examples to the new format (and fixed a duplicate `example` key that broke code generation).\n\nOne design decision worth flagging: for `REGION` I used the existing `LocalityResolver.regionFor(postcode, city)` (postcode-preferred with city fallback) rather than a strict postcode-only lookup. Whenever a postcode is present this is exactly \"derived from the postcode,\" and it keeps locality coherent for the no-postcode case instead of collapsing every such owner to `UNKNOWN`. If the spec intends strictly postcode-only (no city fallback), that's a one-line change in `saveOwner`.",
